div class=\"mark\">✕</div>\n      <p class=\"body\">In French, local Whisper- and Parakeet-style models frequently <b>mis-hear and fall back to English</b> mid-sentence.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"row bad\">\n      <div class=\"mark\">✕</div>\n      <p class=\"body\">Japanese isn't supported at all by most of them.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"row good\">\n      <div class=\"mark\">✓</div>\n      <p class=\"body\">ChatGPT's own dictation handles <b>both</b>, reliably, in daily use.</p>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"spacer\"></div>\n\n    <div class=\"apps\">\n      This isn't a knock on any one app — it's true of local-model dictation\n      generally, Wispr Flow and the offline modes of SuperWhisper and Handy\n      included.\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"spacer\"></div>\n\n    <div class=\"caveat\">\n      Honest caveat: I haven't found an independent benchmark of ChatGPT's own\n      dictation model to point to — it isn't listed on the speech-to-text\n      leaderboards I checked. This is personal, day-to-day experience, not a\n      ranked claim.\n    </div>\n\n  </div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":525217,"output_tokens":1214,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":381,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1214,"cache_read_input_tokens":525217,"cache_creation_input_tokens":381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":381},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cdw6sJ7ko4SUpzPkgtAic","type":"assistant","uuid":"6374b6e6-d957-4be3-b303-517067e289bc","timestamp":"2026-08-11T14:16:05.206Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entryp